// Versão do resumo em inglês. Keywords ficam no main.typ, no parâmetro abstract-palavras.

This research project proposes an evaluation of ModoQAP as a tool that may support self-regulated learning among candidates preparing for Brazilian public examinations. The platform organizes study activities through schedules or study cycles, displays daily tasks, records focused study time, questions and correct answers, consolidates review activities, and presents progress indicators. The study is grounded in the cyclical model of self-regulation, in which learners plan, perform, monitor and revise their strategies. An evaluative case study with a mixed-methods approach will be conducted with adult candidates who will use a stable version of the platform for six weeks. Data collection will combine an initial questionnaire, anonymized usage records, a final perception and usability questionnaire, and semi-structured interviews. The analysis will consider adherence to planning, study frequency, recorded time, question volume and accuracy, completion of reviews, use of goals, and strategy adjustments. Quantitative evidence will be examined descriptively and exploratorily, while interview material will undergo thematic analysis. The project does not seek to attribute public-exam approval outcomes to the platform. Its purpose is to investigate whether and how the available resources contribute to organization, monitoring, perceived control and reflection on study routines. Flashcards, question bank, error notebook, document processing and adaptive tutoring will be treated as product evolution and included only if available in the study version.
